================================================================================
## Let viewers search the graph and use Graph Chat
================================================================================

Context: PermissionMiddleware blocked every POST on domain-scoped paths for
the Viewer role. Explorer search/expand (/dtwin/sync/filter) and Graph Chat
(/dtwin/assistant/chat, /chat/stream, and the agent's query_graphql loopback
to /dtwin/graphql/execute) take a POST body but only read, so a Viewer could
open the Knowledge Graph but not search it or chat. Extract
_viewer_write_blocked so PermissionMiddleware.dispatch does not grow past
the size-budget baseline (186 LOC). Port of 0.9.1 #190.

Changes:

1. src/shared/fastapi/main.py
   Add _VIEWER_READ_ONLY_POSTS (exact paths, POST only) and
   _viewer_write_blocked; skip the viewer write gate for those POSTs.
   Graph Chat writes (/dtwin/nodes/action/request, /confirm) and
   /dtwin/sync/load stay blocked.
2. tests/units/auth/test_permission_middleware.py
   Dispatch tests for all four allowlisted paths (GET/POST allowed;
   PUT/PATCH/DELETE blocked; non-members blocked). Write POSTs and
   prefix-sharing paths stay 403; editors can still POST writes.
   TestViewerWriteBlocked covers _viewer_write_blocked and pins the
   allowlist set.
3. docs/development.md
   Document the Viewer POST exceptions in the enforcement table.

Modified files:
- src/shared/fastapi/main.py
- tests/units/auth/test_permission_middleware.py
- docs/development.md
- changelogs/v0.10.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-10-26.log

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q tests/units/auth/test_permission_middleware.py tests/units/architecture -m "not scenario" → 394 passed. Identical patch on feat/simulation-whatif-sandbox: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" → 9680 passed, 326 skipped, 8 deselected, 0 failed in 54.74s.

================================================================================
## Raise dependency security floors reported by Dependabot
================================================================================

Context: https://github.com/databrickslabs/ontobricks/security/dependabot
listed open alerts across GitPython, mlflow, setuptools, fastmcp/
fastmcp-slim, opentelemetry-api, filelock, and black (Pillow and certifi
were already fixed on this branch in 383c4997). Raised every floor that
has a published fix, citing the GHSA/Dependabot number next to each pin,
matching the existing constraint-dependencies convention. oauthlib 4.0.0
stays blocked (databricks-sql-connector 4.4-4.6 pins oauthlib<4.0.0,
already documented) and nltk has no patched release yet (already
documented, GHSA-8mgp-746c-j5xp).

IMPORTANT — uv.lock NOT regenerated: this sandbox has no network route to
the configured index (pypi-proxy.dev.databricks.com times out mid-TLS-
handshake; public PyPI unreachable too). These floor bumps in
pyproject.toml do NOT yet fix the alerts: Dependabot scans uv.lock, not
pyproject.toml, and the `--frozen` test run below still exercises the OLD
pinned (vulnerable) versions. Someone with working VPN/index access must
run `uv lock` (root) and `cd src/mcp-server && uv lock`, then re-run the
full suite, before this is actually fixed. Same change already applied and
committed on `0.9.1` (same blocker there too).

Changes:

1. pyproject.toml
   Raised floors: mlflow>=3.17.2 (GHSA-2wqp-q3c6-ccj5, GHSA-wqmh-qccw-pqwf),
   black>=26.10.1 (GHSA-cg8m-r9f2-5wm2), fastmcp>=3.4.10
   (GHSA-7xgj-8392-5q4r), gitpython>=3.2.1 (GHSA-83vg-56qc-22m7),
   setuptools>=84.1.0 (GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w). Added constraint-dependencies:
   filelock>=4.2.1 (GHSA-v4x8-3wr5-3wq8 and two more),
   fastmcp-slim>=3.4.10, opentelemetry-api>=1.45.1 (GHSA-xcq7-p3pf-p88h).
2. src/mcp-server/pyproject.toml
   fastmcp>=2.3.1 -> >=3.4.10 (GHSA-7xgj-8392-5q4r). Added
   constraint-dependencies: fastmcp-slim>=3.4.10, opentelemetry-api>=1.45.1.

Modified files:
- pyproject.toml
- src/mcp-server/pyproject.toml
- changelogs/v0.10.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-10-26.log

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario" --ignore=tests/units/api/test_routes.py
→ 9522 passed, 338 skipped, 8 deselected, 0 failed in 39.86s — baseline only,
against the UNCHANGED (old, still-vulnerable) uv.lock. test_routes.py
